  "title": "Dominated Strategy",
  "kind": "definition",
  "status": "staged",
  "href": "strategic_games/dominance/strategic_games_dominance_dominated_strategy.html",
  "body_html": "<h1>Dominated Strategy</h1>\n<p>A strategy $m_i\\in\\Delta(S_i)$ is strictly dominated if there exists\n$\\sigma_i\\in\\Delta(S_i)$ such that\n$$\n  g_i(\\sigma_i,t_{-i})&gt;g_i(m_i,t_{-i})\n  \\quad\\text{for all } t_{-i}\\in S_{-i}.\n$$\nIt is weakly dominated if there exists $\\sigma_i$ such that the same inequalities\nare weak for all $t_{-i}$ and strict for at least one $t_{-i}$.</p>\n<p>For pure strategies, this specializes by identifying $s_i\\in S_i$ with the Dirac\nmass at $s_i$.</p>",
  "proof_html": null,
